title start
kind: research
tags: business-plan research white-accent-evidence
Does white work as the main accent colour for a dark monochrome brand
title end

section start
title start
Abstract
title end
paragraph start
Question: does white work as the main accent for a dark monochrome brand. Method: the same reviews, read for any finding on white. Result: little direct evidence. White served as a neutral control in a colour and performance review, and a cross country study links natural colour associations such as white and purity across populations. Limit: nothing on white accents in social video was found.
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
Introduction
title end
paragraph start
White is the planned main accent, so this page asks whether research supports it.
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
Methods
title end
paragraph start
Read the colour and cognition review and a secondary article on the cross country study of colour associations, looking only for what they say about white.
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
Results
title end
paragraph start
In the colour and cognition review, white was used as the control condition, which treats it as a neutral reference and not as a colour with its own effect.
paragraph end
paragraph start
A cross country study reported through a secondary article found that colour associations rooted in nature, such as white with purity, tend to be shared across populations (Jonauskaite and co-authors, 2020).
paragraph end
paragraph start
Brand studies linked the lightness of a colour to a robust impression (Labrecque and Milne, 2012).
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
Discussion
title end
paragraph start
White on a dark background gives the highest contrast, which helps text overlays stay readable. That is a design fact and was not tested here.
paragraph end
paragraph start
todo: find research on text legibility and contrast on small screens
Not searched yet.
paragraph end
section end

